Dreamer.

2206
01:25:25,940 --> 01:25:27,960
No happy endings for our heroes, though.

2207
01:25:28,380 --> 01:25:36,380
After Teen Boy puts his ride in the ditch there, he needs extra money to pay the
insurance cost and to buy a new disc sander and a couple of gallons of Bondo.

2208
01:25:36,880 --> 01:25:39,580
So, he takes a second job at Carl's Jr.

2209
01:25:40,280 --> 01:25:40,820
Yep, yep.

2210
01:25:40,920 --> 01:25:46,660
And about a week into his new job, he comes to pick her up in his
busted car, wearing a big orange hat and smelling a frying medium.

2211
01:25:46,940 --> 01:25:49,020
And she cools on the whole
relationship immediately.

2212
01:25:49,340 --> 01:25:56,820
Only it drags out painfully for about another month because she doesn't
have the guts to tell the second-rate Matt Latanzi to take the train.

2213
01:25:57,400 --> 01:25:58,060
Yep, yep, yep.

2214
01:25:58,080 --> 01:26:02,379
And finally, she gives him the news through the
drive-up intercom that she just wants to be friends.

2215
01:26:02,380 --> 01:26:10,380
And when the whole restaurant is finally done laughing at the poor Claude, he walks off the job and drives straight
to the municipal liquor store to pick up a quart of lemon-flavored gin and a six-pack of red grape malt duck.

2216
01:26:13,240 --> 01:26:14,800
Uh, hang on.

2217
01:26:14,960 --> 01:26:17,200
You know, Mike might think
that was the happy ending.

2218
01:26:17,620 --> 01:26:20,840
So, you guys really think I'm
a naive Pollyanna, don't you?

2219
01:26:21,020 --> 01:26:22,280
Um, yes, we do.

2220
01:26:22,560 --> 01:26:23,020
Hang on.

2221
01:26:23,080 --> 01:26:24,860
There's more Mr. Rose-colored glasses.

2222
01:26:25,320 --> 01:26:30,099
So, he drinks his way through the whole paper bag,
drives a good 75 yards, and crashes into a pole.

2223
01:26:30,100 --> 01:26:34,000
Well, the car hangs on to the base of the
light pole, so he can't get out of there.

2224
01:26:34,360 --> 01:26:41,080
He thumbs a ride back to his house, but the police arrive about
45 minutes later, wake him up, and give him the breathalyzer.

2225
01:26:41,320 --> 01:26:46,060
He blows a 1.3, so it's off to the
Crowbar Motel for Mike's little pal.

2226
01:26:46,420 --> 01:26:52,260
Well, of course, he calls his former girlfriend to come
pick him up, but Mom answers the phone and hangs up on him.

2227
01:26:52,660 --> 01:26:53,720
Here's one call spent.

2228
01:26:53,980 --> 01:26:57,599
He stays the night at the place with the
striped sunlight, courtesy of the county.

2229
01:26:57,600 --> 01:27:04,080
Soon, he's straining, rubbing alcohol through pieces
of burnt toast he found out behind Zelda's diner.

2230
01:27:04,320 --> 01:27:05,320
Oh, hang on.

2231
01:27:05,400 --> 01:27:05,900
Wait a minute.

2232
01:27:05,940 --> 01:27:07,400
I think that's a touch bleak.

2233
01:27:07,560 --> 01:27:09,036
Well, you know, maybe you're right, Mike.

2234
01:27:09,060 --> 01:27:13,600
Maybe they have a wondrous, frilly
wedding in the frou-frou land of bunnies,

2235
01:27:13,760 --> 01:27:16,680
where magical fairies
blow kisses to the stars,

2236
01:27:16,840 --> 01:27:23,239
and polka-dotted toadstools sing good ship lollipop
to the tiny mice in their little feety pajamas.

2237
01:27:23,240 --> 01:27:25,560
Okay, and there's nothing in between.

2238
01:27:25,740 --> 01:27:30,980
It's either grain alcohol in back alleys, or
a happy world of rodents in feety pajamas.

2239
01:27:31,260 --> 01:27:31,700
Yes!

2240
01:27:32,080 --> 01:27:34,160
I mean, why is that so hard to accept?

2241
01:27:34,300 --> 01:27:35,740
You know, you guys need help.

2242
01:27:35,860 --> 01:27:36,380
You really do.

2243
01:27:36,720 --> 01:27:36,800
Jeez.

2244
01:27:37,100 --> 01:27:38,100
Jeez.

2245
01:27:39,240 --> 01:27:40,240
What's with Mike?

2246
01:27:40,340 --> 01:27:42,039
Grain alcohol through toast.

2247
01:27:42,040 --> 01:27:50,040
So, uh, how'd it go, Joel?

2248
01:27:57,380 --> 01:27:58,960
Uh, it went pretty good.

2249
01:27:59,060 --> 01:28:01,780
I did have some trouble, though,
with the digital switching module.

2250
01:28:01,860 --> 01:28:02,860
It was all greasy.

2251
01:28:03,080 --> 01:28:05,580
Yeah, Mike here tried to
patch it with strips of bacon.

2252
01:28:06,000 --> 01:28:09,079
Oh, well, uh, I've updated
all the necessary systems.

2253
01:28:09,080 --> 01:28:12,960
You shouldn't have any problems for the next 10
years or 20 million miles, whichever comes first.

2254
01:28:13,040 --> 01:28:13,580
Uh, you know what?

2255
01:28:13,640 --> 01:28:15,580
I did want to show you
this fuel filter, though.

2256
01:28:15,620 --> 01:28:17,556
You see all that gunk
that is building up in there?

2257
01:28:17,580 --> 01:28:18,580
Ew, yuck.

2258
01:28:18,660 --> 01:28:20,140
That's got to affect performance.

2259
01:28:20,220 --> 01:28:21,060
Yeah, it sure does.

2260
01:28:21,120 --> 01:28:22,536
It's a good thing I happen along here.

2261
01:28:22,560 --> 01:28:24,700
Now, if you'll just sign
this, uh, I'll be on my way.

2262
01:28:24,900 --> 01:28:26,200
Okay, well, thanks a lot.

2263
01:28:26,660 --> 01:28:27,300
Sorry about that.

2264
01:28:27,301 --> 01:28:28,760
I don't think about my fuel filter.

2265
01:28:28,780 --> 01:28:29,160
No, that's the thing.

2266
01:28:29,220 --> 01:28:29,960
People don't think about it.

2267
01:28:29,960 --> 01:28:30,440
Oh, you know what?

2268
01:28:30,540 --> 01:28:31,140
Pearl's calling.

2269
01:28:31,280 --> 01:28:31,520
Hang on.

2270
01:28:31,540 --> 01:28:32,360
Yeah, you can pay me now.

2271
01:28:32,440 --> 01:28:33,000
Pay me later.

2272
01:28:33,080 --> 01:28:34,080
Yeah, no, I hear you.

2273
01:28:34,500 --> 01:28:34,820
Joel?

2274
01:28:35,340 --> 01:28:36,739
Is that Joel Robinson?

2275
01:28:36,740 --> 01:28:39,380
Brian, look at that.

2276
01:28:39,460 --> 01:28:39,920
It's Frank.

2277
01:28:40,060 --> 01:28:41,720
Frank, how are you, Frank?

2278
01:28:42,180 --> 01:28:42,980
Pretty good.

2279
01:28:43,060 --> 01:28:44,540
Uh, been soul-stealing.

2280
01:28:45,000 --> 01:28:48,780
In fact, you're on my list.

2281
01:28:49,760 --> 01:28:51,860
I'm going to need your soul.

2282
01:28:53,060 --> 01:28:54,940
You know, when, when,
when you get a minute.

2283
01:28:56,280 --> 01:28:56,880
Uh-oh.

2284
01:28:56,980 --> 01:28:58,296
You better get going there, Joel.

2285
01:28:58,320 --> 01:28:59,240
Hey, what about us?

2286
01:28:59,260 --> 01:29:00,060
Can you take us with you?

2287
01:29:00,280 --> 01:29:02,420
Uh, no, I don't really want to.

2288
01:29:02,580 --> 01:29:03,040
Why?

2289
01:29:03,220 --> 01:29:03,420
Why?

2290
01:29:04,080 --> 01:29:05,359
Well, I'll tell you why.

2291
01:29:05,360 --> 01:29:10,280
Because the years I spent here on the Satellite
of Love were the best damn years of my life.

2292
01:29:10,320 --> 01:29:12,799
And I wouldn't want you
mugs to miss a minute of it.

2293
01:29:12,800 --> 01:29:13,080
Really?

2294
01:29:13,340 --> 01:29:14,460
Yeah, really.

2295
01:29:14,580 --> 01:29:15,740
It made a man out of me.

2296
01:29:16,080 --> 01:29:19,800
And maybe, just maybe, if you're
lucky, it'll make a man out of you, too.

2297
01:29:19,920 --> 01:29:20,300
Yeah.

2298
01:29:20,580 --> 01:29:21,580
Yeah, that's it.

2299
01:29:21,800 --> 01:29:23,620
You get going and I'll stay here.

2300
01:29:23,680 --> 01:29:25,100
And I'll get busy being a man.

2301
01:29:25,200 --> 01:29:25,840
That's right.

2302
01:29:25,900 --> 01:29:28,739
I knew there was something
I liked about you, Mike.

2303
01:29:28,740 --> 01:29:33,019
And you two bots, you just keep
them flying and remember Joel, all right?

2304
01:29:33,020 --> 01:29:34,020
All right, Joel.

2305
01:29:34,440 --> 01:29:35,440
Come on, Joel.

2306
01:29:35,640 --> 01:29:35,940
Come on, Joel.

2307
01:29:35,941 --> 01:29:36,979
There goes Joel Robinson.

2308
01:29:36,980 --> 01:29:37,460
Yeah.

2309
01:29:37,840 --> 01:29:39,460
Just find yourself out right out there.

2310
01:29:39,600 --> 01:29:39,800
Yeah.

2311
01:29:39,900 --> 01:29:40,460
All right.

2312
01:29:40,680 --> 01:29:40,980
Yeah.

2313
01:29:40,980 --> 01:29:41,320
Yeah.

2314
01:29:41,940 --> 01:29:42,220
Wow.

2315
01:29:42,620 --> 01:29:43,400
Wow, man.

2316
01:29:43,500 --> 01:29:44,180
Think about it.

2317
01:29:44,181 --> 01:29:47,060
A real man like that allowing
me to find my own way.

2318
01:29:47,120 --> 01:29:47,720
That's right.

2319
01:29:47,800 --> 01:29:49,540
Hey, press the button like a man, Mike.

2320
01:29:49,680 --> 01:29:50,220
Give it a try.

2321
01:29:50,600 --> 01:29:50,920
Okay.

2322
01:29:50,921 --> 01:29:53,240
Oh, yeah.

2323
01:29:53,600 --> 01:29:54,720
Smooth for a man.

2324
01:29:55,580 --> 01:29:56,360
Oh, man.

2325
01:29:56,400 --> 01:29:58,280
I'm going to catch hell from my boss.

2326
01:29:58,360 --> 01:30:00,180
I haven't brought back any souls yet.

2327
01:30:00,400 --> 01:30:03,060
Oh, Frank, please take my soul.

2328
01:30:03,140 --> 01:30:04,360
I'm not going to be using it.

2329
01:30:04,480 --> 01:30:05,340
Oh, no.

2330
01:30:05,460 --> 01:30:06,600
I couldn't, really.

2331
01:30:06,820 --> 01:30:07,460
Well, hang on.

2332
01:30:07,580 --> 01:30:08,580
Hey, brain guy.

2333
01:30:09,060 --> 01:30:09,320
Yo.

2334
01:30:09,440 --> 01:30:12,100
Oh, Frank here is going
to be stealing your soul.

2335
01:30:12,400 --> 01:30:13,260
Oh, I'm sorry.

2336
01:30:13,340 --> 01:30:14,840
You're barking up the wrong albino.

2337
01:30:15,000 --> 01:30:16,000
I'm just a brain.

2338
01:30:16,300 --> 01:30:17,980
100% soul free.

2339
01:30:18,460 --> 01:30:18,980
Sorry.

2340
01:30:18,981 --> 01:30:26,981
Would someone maybe like to steal my soul?

2341
01:30:28,940 --> 01:30:29,420
Really?

2342
01:30:29,540 --> 01:30:30,540
Are you sure it's okay?

2343
01:30:30,780 --> 01:30:33,720
This old soul, please do
me the favor of stealing it.

2344
01:30:34,300 --> 01:30:34,780
Wow.

2345
01:30:35,020 --> 01:30:35,420
Okay.

2346
01:30:35,820 --> 01:30:36,120
Come on.

2347
01:30:36,320 --> 01:30:38,500
Please roll the old miracle.

2348
01:30:39,060 --> 01:30:40,580
It's slipping out now.

2349
01:30:41,460 --> 01:30:42,460
There.

2350
01:30:42,760 --> 01:30:45,060
You'll be top soul stealer in no time.

2351
01:30:45,600 --> 01:30:46,080
I know.

2352
01:30:46,180 --> 01:30:49,200
Let's play ring toss with your soul.

2353
01:30:52,420 --> 01:30:54,599
I knew these two would get along.

2354
